# The support of the quotient of the structure sheaf by an ideal sheaf

Let `X` be a locally ringed space and let `j : J ⟶ 𝒪_X` be a sheaf of ideals, presented as a
morphism of sheaves of `𝒪_X`-modules into the structure sheaf. The quotient `𝒪_X / J` as a
sheaf of rings, and the description of its support, are the repository's canonical
declarations in `Stacks.ClosedImmersion`
(`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ClosedImmersion/ClosedSubspace.lean` and
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ClosedImmersion/ClosedSubspaceExistence.lean`); they are
re-exported here and nothing is redeclared.

The support is described stalkwise: a point `x` lies in it exactly when no local section of `J`
has a unit germ at `x`. Off the support the stalk of the quotient is the zero ring; on the
support it is a local ring, and the quotient map is a local homomorphism there.

## Main declarations

* `quotientSupport` is the support of `𝒪_X / J`, and `quotientSupport_isClosed` says it is
  closed, being the complement of the union of the basic opens of the sections of `J`.
* `quotientIdeal` is the ideal of `𝒪_X(U)` generated by the sections of `J` over `U`.
* `quotientRingPresheaf` and `quotientRingSheaf` are `𝒪_X / J` as a presheaf and as a sheaf of
  rings, the latter being the sheafification of the former, and `quotientRingSheafMap` is the
  quotient map `𝒪_X ⟶ 𝒪_X / J`.
* `quotientRingSheaf_stalk_isTerminal_of_not_mem_support`: off the support the stalk of
  `𝒪_X / J` is the zero ring.
* `quotientRingSheafMap_stalk_surjective`: the quotient map is surjective on stalks at every
  point.
* `quotientRingSheaf_stalk_isLocalRing_of_mem_support` and
  `quotientRingSheafMap_stalk_isLocalHom`: on the support the stalk is a local ring and the
  quotient map is a local homomorphism.

## Implementation notes

These names were originally a second, content-identical copy of the canonical declarations,
which were `private` and so unreachable; the bodies agreed line for line but the constants were
distinct, which silently made everything stated here non-composable with the canonical
development and with the Tag 01HN attribute it carries. The canonical declarations are now
public and this file aliases them, so the two spellings are one constant.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01HN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01HN)
-/

